
== arrays and records ==
prices                                   9.99, 0.5, 120, 3.10, 7
record field                             1.20
after += 0.05d                           1.25
nested arithmetic                        12.50

== sorting ==
table.sort default order                 0.5, 3.10, 7, 9.99, 120
descending                               120, 9.99, 7, 3.10, 0.5
smallest first                           1.4
the three equal values are adjacent      true
sorted records                           b a c

== aggregation ==
sum                                      140.59
min                                      0.5
max                                      120
average                                  28.118
min(...) / max(...) variadic             0.5 120
table.unpack                             5

== tables of decimals as maps (values only) ==
apple                                    0.75
pear                                     0.75

== decimals cannot be table keys ==
t[1.5d] = 1                              error: table index is a decimal
rawset(t, 1.5d, 1)                       error: table index is a decimal
t[1.5d] (a read is just nil)             nil
workaround: key by tostring              1
note: tostring keeps the scale           false

== table.find ==
table.find(prices, 120d) (not supported yet) nil
a loop with == works                     3

== functions: arguments, returns, varargs, closures ==
varargs sum                              6.6
closure after 3 calls                    0.3
multiple returns                         2.25, 5.5
pcall passes decimals through            1.25
coroutine passes decimals through        3.5

== strings: no coercion, but interpolation works ==
string.format('%s', d)                   error: invalid argument #2 to 'format' (string expected, got decimal)
string.format('%d', d)                   error: invalid argument #2 to 'format' (number expected, got decimal)
string.format('%.2f', d)                 error: invalid argument #2 to 'format' (number expected, got decimal)
'total ' .. d                            error: attempt to concatenate string with decimal
string.format with tostring              1.5
interpolation                            total 1.5
string.format('%.2f', tonumber(d))       1.50
print(d) shows scale                     1.50

== other library functions refuse decimals ==
math.max(1d, 2d)                         error: invalid argument #1 to 'max' (number expected, got decimal)
math.floor(1.5d)                         error: invalid argument #1 to 'floor' (number expected, got decimal)
math.abs(-1d)                            error: invalid argument #1 to 'abs' (number expected, got decimal)
tonumber(1.5d)                           nil
#1.5d                                    error: attempt to get length of a decimal value
select('#', 1.5d)                        1
